---
/**
 * Contact form, posting to Netlify Forms (D3).
 *
 * Replaces Drupal's `contact_message` form plus the `tome_netlify` module that
 * rewrote it for static hosting. Same three fields and same recipient; the
 * honeypot survives, the captcha stays absent, as the old config had it.
 *
 * How this works with no server: Netlify parses the deployed HTML at build
 * time, finds `data-netlify`, and registers a form by its `name`. Submissions
 * post back to the site and Netlify captures them. Two consequences worth
 * knowing:
 *
 *  - The hidden `form-name` input must be present and must match `name`, or the
 *    submission is rejected: the POST is handled by name, not by URL.
 *  - It only works on a real Netlify deploy. Locally, submitting this form 404s;
 *    that is expected, not a bug to chase.
 *
 * `action` sends the visitor to the same thank-you page the Drupal form used,
 * so that URL keeps working.
 */
---

<form
  class="form"
  name="contatti"
  method="POST"
  action="/contatti/messaggio-inviato/"
  data-netlify="true"
  netlify-honeypot="bot-field"
>
  <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="contatti" />

  {
    /* The honeypot: hidden from people, tempting to bots. Not `display: none`
      via CSS alone: `hidden` keeps it out of the tab order too. */
  }
  <p hidden>
    <label>Non compilare questo campo: <input name="bot-field" /></label>
  </p>

  <p class="field">
    <label for="contact-name">Il tuo nome</label>
    <input id="contact-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required />
  </p>

  <p class="field">
    <label for="contact-email">Il tuo indirizzo e-mail</label>
    <input id="contact-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required />
  </p>

  <p class="field">
    <label for="contact-message">Messaggio</label>
    <textarea id="contact-message" name="message" rows="6" required></textarea>
  </p>

  {
    /*
      The Art. 13 notice, at the point of collection. A line and a link, not a
      checkbox: the lawful basis for answering a message someone chose to send
      is the message, not consent, and a tick box would ask for permission the
      club does not need while implying the opposite.
    */
  }
  <p class="form__notice">
    I dati che invii servono solo a risponderti. Vedi{' '}
    <a href="/privacy">l'informativa privacy</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    <button class="button" type="submit">Invia</button>
  </p>
</form>

<style>
  .form__notice {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    max-width: var(--prose-width);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
  }

  /* `.field` and its controls are a global primitive: see global.css. */
</style>
